@startuml
!include style.puml
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

participant ":EqmManager" as Manager
participant ":LoanHandler" as Handler
participant "LocalDate" as Date <<Java API>>
participant "LoanStorage" as Store <<utility>>

Manager -> Handler: addLoan("loan id/001 b/002 due/31-10-26")
activate Handler
Handler -> Handler: parseLoanCommand(input)
activate Handler
Handler -> Handler: parseLoanArguments(arguments, clock)
note right of Handler
Validate required IDs and due date first.
This example omits the entire issued/ field.
end note
Handler -> Date: now(clock)
Date --> Handler: current local date
note right of Handler
Use date.atStartOfDay() as issuedDate.
Reject issuedDate after dueDate.
end note
Handler --> Handler: parsed loan with explicit dates
deactivate Handler
note right of Handler
Check item availability and loan ID limit;
create identified loan and proposed list.
end note
Handler -> Store: save(...)
Store --> Handler: saved successfully
note right of Handler
Publish loan, advance counters and
attach the original equipment object.
end note
Handler --> Manager: added loan
deactivate Handler
note over Handler, Date
Explicit issued/ values use strict parsing without reading the clock.
Stored records always require both dates.
end note
@enduml
